Converts floating-point numbers exactly: printf's %e, %f, %g and %a,
strtod(3) and its kin, and scanf's floating-point conversions use musl
1.2.5's code (ports/mlibc/musl, which build.sh copies to
options/internal/include/mlibc). mlibc's own went through uint64_t and
pow() or summed digits in the result's type, so printf("%f", 1e20) and
strtod("1e308") came out wrong. Meant for upstream.

